<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iblul-Il</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/24th-century-bce">24th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iblul-Il was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in the twenty-fourth century BCE. A letter found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> records his campaigns against towns in Ebla's sphere along the middle Euphrates and in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, after which Ebla paid tribute to Mari. A statue of him with a dedicatory inscription was found at Mari, and he is one of the best-attested rulers of its Early Dynastic city.</p></div>
